From a2f3663e0f04e67c77d25962880d0936a7d849b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] regions: add per-output snap regions

A <region> may name one output with output="<connector>". An output named
by at least one region gets only its own regions, a snap layout; every
other output keeps the regions without an output attribute, as before.
An empty output is the same as none and a name without an output has no
effect. Region names only need to be unique per output, and several
<regions> elements add up.

On an output with a layout, the cardinal SnapToEdge and ToggleSnapToEdge
actions move the window through its regions: a window in a region goes
to the nearest region beyond it in that direction, preferring regions
that overlap it on the other axis, and past the last one to the adjacent
output (its region at the shared edge, or the opposite edge of an output
without a layout). Any other window goes to the region furthest in that
direction, ties going to the one nearest the window. ToggleSnapToEdge
restores the untiled position where SnapToEdge would change outputs. A
window snapped to an edge of an output without a layout that is moved
onto an output with one enters it by a region instead of a half.

Dragging a window to an edge of an output with a layout offers the
region nearest the cursor instead of the half, quarter or maximized
target; the overlay shows it with the usual edge delay.

Fullscreen windows and windows managed by tiling are left as they were.
Hotplug, reconfigure and disabled outputs reuse the existing evacuation
and name matching.
---
 docs/labwc-actions.5.scd |  27 ++++
 docs/labwc-config.5.scd  |  21 ++++
 docs/rc.xml.all          |   9 ++
 include/regions.h        |  21 ++++
 src/action.c             |   5 +
 src/config/rcxml.c       |  11 +-
 src/interactive.c        |   6 +-
 src/overlay.c            |  23 +++-
 src/regions.c            | 262 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 9 files changed, 380 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
index 3414247..70db537 100644
--- a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
+++ b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
@@ -116,6 +116,33 @@ Actions are used in menus and keyboard/mouse bindings.
 	ToggleSnapToEdge additionally toggles the active window between
 	tiled to the given direction and its untiled position.
 
+	On an output with its own snap regions (*<region output="">*, see
+	labwc-config(5)), *up*, *down*, *left* and *right* move the window
+	through those regions instead and *combine* has no effect:
+
+	- A window snapped to one of the output's regions moves to the
+	  nearest region whose centre lies beyond the current one in the
+	  given direction, preferring regions that overlap it on the other
+	  axis. Without such a region it moves to the adjacent output in that
+	  direction: onto the region nearest to the shared edge if that
+	  output has its own regions, otherwise snapped to the opposite edge.
+	  Without an adjacent output nothing happens.
+
+	- Any other window (floating, maximized or snapped to an edge) is
+	  snapped to the region lying furthest in the given direction; among
+	  regions equally far, the one nearest to the window's centre.
+
+	- ToggleSnapToEdge does the same, except that where SnapToEdge would
+	  move the window to another output it restores the window's untiled
+	  position instead.
+
+	A window snapped to the right edge of an output without its own
+	regions that is snapped to the right again moves to the adjacent
+	output as usual; if that output has its own regions, the window is
+	placed in the region nearest to the shared edge instead of its left
+	half (likewise for the other directions). Fullscreen windows and
+	windows managed by tiling keep the behaviour described above.
+
 *<action name="ToggleSnapToRegion" region="value" />*++
 *<action name="SnapToRegion" region="value" />*
 	Resize and move active window according to the given region.
diff --git a/docs/labwc-config.5.scd b/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
index d011a81..b9e7194 100644
--- a/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
+++ b/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
@@ -665,6 +665,27 @@ extending outward from the snapped edge.
 	Windows can either be snapped to regions by keeping a keyboard modifier
 	pressed while moving a window (Ctrl, Alt, Shift, Logo) or by using the
 	SnapToRegion action. By default there are no regions defined.
+	Several *<regions>* elements add up.
+
+*<regions><region name="" output="HDMI-A-1" x="" y="" width="" height="">*
+	The optional *output* attribute gives a region to one output only,
+	named by its connector, such as "HDMI-A-1" or "DP-1". An output named
+	by at least one region uses its own regions as a snap layout and does
+	not get the regions without an *output* attribute. Outputs that no
+	region names keep all regions without an *output* attribute. An empty
+	*output* is the same as leaving it out; a name that matches no output
+	has no effect. Region names only need to be unique per output.
+
+	On an output with a snap layout, the cardinal SnapToEdge and
+	ToggleSnapToEdge actions move the window between the layout's regions
+	(see labwc-actions(5)), and dragging a window to an output edge snaps
+	it to the layout's region nearest to the cursor instead of an edge,
+	corner or maximized position. The overlay then shows that region,
+	with the usual edge delay and region theme.
+
+	When an output is removed or the regions change, windows snapped to a
+	region move to the region of the same name on their new output, or
+	return to their untiled size if there is none.
 
 ## WORKSPACES
 
